## Why This Is Asked
Tests planning of safe, multi-region rollout with feature flags and clear rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Progressive rollout
- Feature flags
- Telemetry and SLO-aligned signals
- Cache invalidation/versioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for rollout gating
const enabled = getFlag("new_api_behavior");
if (enabled && regions.includes(currentRegion)) {
  useNewBehavior();
} else {
  useOldBehavior();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this if some regions have mandatory latency budgets?
- How would you integrate with an incident response playbook?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes cross-region consistency, edge-scale reliability, and clear runbooks for failures.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed consensus with multi-DC Raft and quorum tuning
- Partition tolerance and per-tenant sharding
- Idempotent, sequenced operations
- Anti-entropy reconciliation and safe replay
- Observability, alerting, and rollback runbooks

## Code Example
```javascript
// simple idempotent write with sequence tokens
function applyWrite(store, key, value, token) {
  const cur = store[key];
  if (!cur || token > cur.token) {
    store[key] = { value, token };
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the reconciliation path under partitions?
- What metrics signal reconciliation backlog and potential data loss?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design automated degradation with controlled risk during external dependency pressure and multi-region operation.

## Key Concepts
- Circuit breakers and failover
- Per-region degradation strategies
- Idempotent queues and exactly-once delivery
- Canary and synthetic testing
- Rollback criteria and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for circuit breaker state machine
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold, resetTime) {
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.resetTime = resetTime;
    this.failures = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }
  onFailure() {
    this.failures++;
    if (this.failures > this.threshold) this.state = 'OPEN';
  }
  canRequest() { return this.state !== 'OPEN'; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for multi-tenant services with mixed SLIs?
- How would you validate degradation paths in canaries without impacting customers?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design isolation, backpressure controls, and controlled degradation under burst traffic, with clear rollback criteria and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation via edge throttling and per-tenant queues
- Backpressure mechanisms and circuit breakers
- Safe degradation strategies and cache fallbacks
- Telemetry: p95/p99 latency, error rate, queue depth, saturation
- Clear rollback criteria and automation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple token bucket limiter
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  allow() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= 1) {
      this.tokens -= 1;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate plan with load tests and synthetic surges?
- What metrics and thresholds would trigger a rollback, and how would you automate it?
